path to display camra  : ":/usr/share/prophesee_driver/samples" 

4 exec file for the prophese camera : 
prophesee_raw_to_video
prophesee_viewer
prophesee_raw_info
prophesee_raw_to_dat


press space bar to start recording usign prophesse_viewer exec file , there is a command line option --output( or -o)
default value is ( filename_to_log_into = "data.raw" ) 
other option : 
desc.add_options()
    ("serial,s",  ...)   // choose a specific camera
    ("filename,f", ...)  // read from a .raw file instead of live camera
    ("biases,b",  ...)   // load a specific .bias file
    ("max-rate",  ...)   // max event rate limit [kev/s]
    ("output,o",  ...)   // path of recording file (data.raw by default)
    ("roi,r",     ...)   // hardware ROI: x y width height

Bias file : 
in prohesee event camera each pixel is a circuit that decide when to fire an event based on local contrast changes

To control how that circuit behaves (recording condition ) , the camera hardware exposes a set of analog bias parameters 

example of .bias file : 
